### name: lim.deep-copy-is-independent
--- note
Assignment copies by value all the way down, so no two variables share structure.
--- source
A[1]["x"] = 1; B = A; B[1]["x"] = 9; A[1]["x"]
--- expect
num 1
===
### name: lim.interp-applies-scalar-context-to-list
--- note
Interpolation lowers to `&`, so it applies scalar context — a list yields its
first element rather than the list.
--- source
"{(7, 8)}"
--- expect
text "7"
===
### name: lim.prefix-depth-neg
--- note
Prefix operators recurse into themselves without passing through the two
functions that track nesting, so a chain of them used to be counted by nothing
at all. It reached the host's own stack limit instead of E_DEPTH: a RangeError
in JS and a *segfault* in C++, from a rule that is only `-` repeated. The
position is the operator that crossed the limit, not the start of the chain.
--- source
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------1
--- expect
error E_DEPTH at 1:200
===
### name: lim.prefix-depth-not
--- note
The same hole, through the other prefix operator. NOT is four columns wide, so
the limit falls at a different column than it does for `-` — which is the point
of pinning both.
--- source
NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT NOT TRUE
